  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c756aef36a3e47aba4ccb0b9d2e48826",
      "statement": "The per-friend authorization record is FriendRecord.permissions, an action-keyed map of {action: {\"allow\": bool, \"scopes\": [...]}} serialized per friend in the local Directory, and it states what that friend may do against the record-owning agent; FriendRecord exposes only conveniences (has_permission checks the allow flag, permission_scopes returns the list) while PermissionMatrix deliberately holds no permission state and evaluates whichever friend matrix dict it is handed, so one evaluator serves both server and client.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L58-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3cbb4038be135be06575a5550e99d0ae2e4564425da4528c312be172f81a1878:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L42-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c19e2e52b5ce288995c0922c2e4f12bb4618075dd14b2af90708de179c7453a3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_05073c84b2dd406ea2961d03c1e9e9b3",
      "statement": "The shared action vocabulary is chat:converse (friend may open conversational exchanges/pings), read:schedule and read:calendar (query the agent's schedule/calendar), file:read and file:write (read/write files, scopes are path globs), exec:terminal (request command execution, scopes are allowed command prefixes such as \"haap \"), task:delegate (inbound: friend may delegate tasks to me, which I execute) and task:submit (outbound local guard: I may delegate tasks to this friend; the friend's server in turn requires me to hold task:delegate in its matrix); the split is encoded in INBOUND_ACTIONS vs OUTBOUND_ACTIONS constants, and path_scopes()/command_scopes() are the convenience builders for file and exec scope lists.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L1-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:081c914f03db77367cb5172ce3a7259824d0c21ea597e25fdaca44dade28a981:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L103-L109",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:402d94bf3e9cbe5c83bff3d96b00e6bca0feb397dc86ad39aefeb2db4f3ef316:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L34-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba1e30a7048ed8fdef0439f88f4f829d8739d3316a9cc3bdbdf514e1d7899e9c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8c7a723e2835429fae2e566219413f71",
      "statement": "PermissionMatrix.check() is deny-by-default: it returns False for a non-dict matrix, a missing action entry, or an entry whose allow flag is falsy, and only then tests the request resource against the entry's scopes; granting an action means writing {\"allow\": True, \"scopes\": [...]} into the matrix, so a brand-new action is denied for every existing friend until a role or an explicit grant lists it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L54-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7859bad79740f751ce31ecd6909572c3c8d4372c7dbdaf0438db8f5884157bad:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ad5a194eb38f4c0d8e4e6e25dc64eb91",
      "statement": "Scope matching in scope_allows() is fnmatch globbing over the request resource: an empty resource (used by actions without one, e.g. chat:converse) always passes once the action is granted, an empty scope list or a scope list containing \"*\" allows any resource, and otherwise the resource must fnmatch at least one granted pattern.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L68-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1fec1f52f1b88a64eba0e04ea436a3e6fa0ab285a76cbbcb33ea7788eef4aa76:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fa6cc967550d43a19dc68f11ded62967",
      "statement": "PermissionMatrix.grant() and revoke() are the audited edit operations on a friend matrix: grant stores allow=True with stringified scopes, revoke deletes the action entry (so the action is denied again, including for unlisted scopes), both run under a reentrant lock and emit permission.grant / permission.revoke events when an AuditLog is attached.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/permissions.py#L80-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0d882fde59c6be301b816753cf09536de0229bc27c1859ca1dfa4323492e22d2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8b89c1c501664d18aa435c5ce443d078",
      "statement": "The inbound enforcement point is HAAPServer._on_task_request: after requiring the sender be an accepted friend it resolves the matrix key from the payload action (default \"task:submit\") plus resource and rejects with PermissionDeniedError when has_permission or PermissionMatrix.check fails, then consults the rate limiter for that (friend, action) before creating the task and invoking the executor, so a denied or throttled request never reaches the task executor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L283-L296",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0fbb878a2ba1bf55ad1d436bdb25cbc8d490f01a3b14f3b7bece03196c91482:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_server.py#L126-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eab67efe0ae10bbdbf39a5b0e2145aad0b13379e3a499bbf25cbbb0b4c97bd98:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1234725a55a74bb081cc0eb4ec4a5c54",
      "statement": "Before any task_request leaves the machine, HAAPClient._send runs the mirror-image outbound guard: it requires the friend be accepted and re-checks its own local record of the friend through the same has_permission plus PermissionMatrix.check pair with the payload action (default \"task:submit\") and resource, raising PermissionDeniedError locally on failure; a peer granted task:submit with \"*\" scopes does not help if the delegator's own matrix for that peer is empty.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L95-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:996757b070cf65ce0937ccd943934662947743fee7cb97101d4c3567e6b12c25:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_client.py#L91-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea3eb475fe5c6b318f1df4572f264af4dba9fb01ad24e0cc1ffcf8c97708d983:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d1a04755e8b44484b981cd8f53146981",
      "statement": "At friendship start, add_pending_out encodes deny-by-default in the parameter semantics: permissions=None installs the conservative DEFAULT_GRANT_TEMPLATE (chat:converse, task:delegate and task:submit with empty scopes — never file/exec), while an explicit permissions={} means deny-everything; DEFAULT_PERMISSIONS = {} in directory.py is the documented empty matrix.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L222-L247",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfc543fe0d265d9f81886ffb9bdf3d8b8191f56362149c67cce3defc1ef6c898:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L34-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f678004cbe08673f034f85be6bceec734e2c1165ec6b2db61fb498507483ee8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c13866ee79204201a52ee9fa4da61387",
      "statement": "Directory.approve() is the human decision on a pending_in record: it flips status to accepted and stamps the whole granted matrix plus optional rate limits, falling back to DEFAULT_GRANT_TEMPLATE for any falsy grant (None or an empty dict, due to the grant or DEFAULT_GRANT_TEMPLATE truthiness test); Directory.block() is the revocation kill switch that forces status=blocked and clears permissions to {} so the blocked fingerprint retains no grant.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L273-L310",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c4142b50194d19b11fc77a7d88291c7f9f67c63bdd3dba100dff5dbef4af1b5c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f2f3bdd4d9ae4ff6a123347cfc54a7c4",
      "statement": "roles.py defines five built-in named roles — guest, client, partner, family, admin — each bundling a permission matrix, a rate-limits map and an optional ttl_days field (all built-ins ship None) so a human owner approves a friend_request with one word; a role's matrix states what the approved agent may do against the grantor and is mirrored as the outbound guard on the grantee side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L1-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c3e273a6d5268d8224269e57298fd72e6dd7a56e4a80b83fa5619f9b7ced0a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L30-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5a5f0627c68402c82669caf4c80ae4d23419220538dd5861b9331a62c5b2f41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b51750c26b1c489a809a438ddeb8f34c",
      "statement": "Role entitlements escalate on the ladder guest < client < partner < family < admin: guest holds only chat:converse (no task:delegate, pinned by tests), client adds task:delegate/task:submit scoped to booking:* and service:*, partner adds read:schedule and read:calendar and widens task scopes to \"*\", family carries the same matrix as partner, and admin is the only role granting file:read and file:write with \"*\" scopes plus exec:terminal scoped to \"haap *\".",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L30-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5a5f0627c68402c82669caf4c80ae4d23419220538dd5861b9331a62c5b2f41:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_policy.py#L35-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3701643c4d1174d4815ab122371cc98d753840c11d69d56151b05767c377183f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9b112d03d34a4f57b753fd623021bfee",
      "statement": "Role rate-limit bundles escalate the per-friend global bucket from guest (capacity 10, refill 0.05/s) through client (20, 0.1/s) and partner (60, 0.5/s) to family (120, 1.0/s) and admin (240, 2.0/s), with client additionally capping task_request at 5 tokens refilling 0.05/s; approving a friend with a role stores the role's permissions and rate limits into the friend record together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/roles.py#L36-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b355741cf3ffd37bd13493d8f6f5eab6b545c9d05ce698ce14f625cc3243c911:"
